<VI _name="lvdiag_probe_v8.vi" description="Phase 0 step 8 probe\3A adds the object label. {LV.Node} Label and {LV.Constant} Label each need their own downcast and both return a Text reference\2C so {LV.Text} Text turns it into a string. The two reads are concatenated - whichever does not apply yields empty. Emits diagramId/objectId/class/label. Step 7 description follows. Step 7 probe\3A full-depth traversal plus structure boundary objects. Extends step 6 with {LV.Structure} Tunnels[] and {LV.Loop} Shift Registers[] behind their own downcasts\2C emitted as B/structureId/objectId/class rows. Those are the objects step 4 saw as unresolved owner ids and that step 5 found are NOT in the inner diagram - they belong to the structure itself. Step 6 description follows. Full-depth traversal. A While Loop drives a worklist of diagram references - seeded with Build Array in element mode on the top-level Block Diagram\2C which is how the array gets its type without an empty-array constant. Each pass indexes one diagram\2C emits its objects\2C and appends every child diagram found via To More Specific Class -&gt; {LV.Structure} Diagrams[]. The per-pass worklist accumulator is initialised from the CURRENT worklist rather than an empty array\2C which solves the same typing problem a second time. Stops when the index reaches the worklist size\2C so nesting depth is unbounded. Emits diagramId/objectId/class per object. Drive it with RunVIAsTopLevel and two string inputs\2C both full paths.">
